================================================================================
1. DEFINITIONS & RETROACTIVE SCOPE
================================================================================
- "The Mod" refers to OStimNet across all past, present, and future versions,
  releases, tags, and git commits, including its SKSE C++ source code and
  compiled binaries (OStimNet.dll), Creation Kit plugin (TT_OStimNet.esp),
  Papyrus scripts (Scripts/Source/*.psc and compiled .pex files), SkyrimNet
  bundle/prompt/action definitions (SKSE/Plugins/SkyrimNet/), JSON/INI/YAML
  configurations and animation descriptions (SKSE/Plugins/OStimNet/), interface
  translation files (Interface/), documentation, and all associated assets in
  this repository.
- "Author" refers to tetherball88.
- "Public API Files" refers strictly to:
  1. Scripts/Source/OStimNet.psc

================================================================================
2. PERMITTED USES (WHAT YOU MAY DO)
================================================================================
Subject to the restrictions in Section 3, the Author grants you the following
non-exclusive, royalty-free permissions:

a) Personal Use:
   You may download, inspect, and compile the source code for your own personal,
   private gameplay and testing.

b) Contributions (GitHub Forks & Pull Requests):
   In accordance with the GitHub Terms of Service, you may fork this repository
   on GitHub, make modifications in your fork for testing or development, and
   submit Pull Requests, bug reports, or issues back to the official repository.

c) Compatibility Patches, Add-ons & Integrations:
   You may create and publish independent compatibility patches, JSON/YAML
   configuration presets, animation description packs, SkyrimNet prompt/action
   extensions, or third-party mods that interact with The Mod, PROVIDED THAT:
   - Your patch or mod requires the official release of OStimNet as an external
     dependency (master/requirement); and
   - Your upload does NOT bundle, repackage, or redistribute OStimNet.dll,
     TT_OStimNet.esp, OStimNet SkyrimNet bundles, or OStimNet core scripts
     (except for the Public API Files covered in Section 4).

d) Translations:
   You may create and publish translations of The Mod (such as translated string
   files, JSON/YAML localization files, prompt translations, or ESP text-only
   translation patches), PROVIDED THAT:
   - The translation is distributed strictly as a translation-only patch that
     requires the original OStimNet mod to function;
   - It does not bundle OStimNet.dll or the full mod archive; and
   - Clear credit and a link back to the official OStimNet page are provided.

================================================================================
3. PROHIBITED USES (WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO)
================================================================================
Without prior written permission from the Author, you may NOT:

a) Redistribute or Re-upload:
   Upload, host, mirror, or distribute The Mod (in whole or in part, whether
   unmodified or modified, from any version or commit) as a standalone mod, fork,
   or replacement package on Nexus Mods, Steam Workshop, Bethesda.net, Discord,
   Patreon, LoversLab, or any other website or platform.

b) Plagiarize or Rebrand:
   Copy substantial portions of the C++ implementation, Papyrus service scripts,
   SkyrimNet prompt/action definitions, or ESP records to publish under your own
   name or as a competing/derivative standalone mod.

c) Commercial Use or Paywalling:
   Sell, rent, sublicense, or place The Mod, any patch, or any derivative work
   behind a paywall, donation lock, or commercial subscription.

